{"plan":{"schema":"whiteboard-plan/1","planId":"wj_05571143845b4930969cfc236f685e9f","revision":1,"goal":"Understand that gradient descent finds a minimum by repeatedly stepping opposite the slope, and see two steps worked out on f(x) = x squared.","audience":"a curious learner","durationSeconds":30,"language":"en","voice":"whiteboard-default-v1","quality":"whiteboard-1080p-v1","sourceRefs":[],"scenes":[{"id":"s1","startFrame":0,"endFrame":360,"learningPoint":"Gradient descent finds a function's lowest point by repeatedly stepping opposite the slope, which means downhill.","visualIntent":"Axes with the curve f(x) = x squared, sampled at 15 points from x = -3.5 to 3.5. A dot at x = 3 (height 9), a short tangent line there, and an arrow pointing downhill toward x = 0, labelled 'step opposite the slope'.","narrationSummary":"Gradient descent finds the lowest point of a curve by repeatedly taking small steps downhill, opposite the slope.","facts":[{"text":"starting point x","value":3,"provenance":"claim"},{"text":"f(3) = 3 squared","value":9,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"minimum of x squared is at x","value":0,"provenance":"computed"}],"illustration":false},{"id":"s2","startFrame":360,"endFrame":900,"learningPoint":"Each step uses new x = x minus step size times slope, and the steps shrink as the slope flattens near the minimum.","visualIntent":"Written rule: 'slope = 2x', 'new x = x − 0.25 × slope'. Line 1: 'x = 3, slope 6, new x = 3 − 1.5 = 1.5'. Line 2: 'x = 1.5, slope 3, new x = 1.5 − 0.75 = 0.75'. On the same curve, dots at x = 3, 1.5, 0.75 joined by arrows, heights 9, 2.25, 0.5625 labelled.","narrationSummary":"For x squared, the slope is 2x. Starting at 3, slope 6; times step size 0.25 moves us to 1.5. Then slope 3 moves us to 0.75, approaching zero.","facts":[{"text":"step size","value":0.25,"provenance":"claim"},{"text":"slope at x = 3 (2 × 3)","value":6,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"new x after step 1 (3 − 0.25 × 6)","value":1.5,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"slope at x = 1.5 (2 × 1.5)","value":3,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"new x after step 2 (1.5 − 0.25 × 3)","value":0.75,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"f(1.5)","value":2.25,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"f(0.75)","value":0.5625,"provenance":"computed"}],"illustration":false}],"substitutions":[],"limitations":["Uses a one-variable curve, x squared; real uses have many variables, but the step rule is the same.","The starting point 3 and step size 0.25 are illustrative numbers chosen to keep the arithmetic simple.","Only two steps are shown; the process continues until the steps become tiny."]},"scenes":[{"schema":"whiteboard-scene/1","sceneId":"s1","primitives":[{"id":"xaxis","kind":"arrow","color":"#333333","width":3,"x1":360,"y1":920,"x2":1580,"y2":920},{"id":"yaxis","kind":"arrow","color":"#333333","width":3,"x1":960,"y1":920,"x2":960,"y2":130},{"id":"xlab","kind":"text","color":"#333333","width":2,"x":1600,"y":905,"size":40,"text":"x"},{"id":"flab","kind":"text","color":"#1f4e9e","width":2,"x":990,"y":140,"size":40,"text":"f(x) = x²"},{"id":"curve","kind":"graph","color":"#1f4e9e","width":5,"x":360,"y":140,"w":1200,"h":780,"domain":[-3.5,3.5],"range":[0,12.25],"points":[[-3.5,12.25],[-3,9],[-2.5,6.25],[-2,4],[-1.5,2.25],[-1,1],[-0.5,0.25],[0,0],[0.5,0.25],[1,1],[1.5,2.25],[2,4],[2.5,6.25],[3,9],[3.5,12.25]]},{"id":"mindot","kind":"ellipse","color":"#2a8a3e","width":4,"cx":960,"cy":920,"rx":12,"ry":12},{"id":"minlab","kind":"text","color":"#2a8a3e","width":2,"x":830,"y":975,"size":40,"text":"minimum at x = 0"},{"id":"dot","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d0402b","width":5,"cx":1474,"cy":347,"rx":14,"ry":14},{"id":"dotlab","kind":"text","color":"#d0402b","width":2,"x":1515,"y":320,"size":40,"text":"x = 3, f = 9"},{"id":"tangent","kind":"line","color":"#e08a00","width":4,"x1":1423,"y1":462,"x2":1526,"y2":232},{"id":"step","kind":"arrow","color":"#d0402b","width":6,"x1":1400,"y1":370,"x2":1200,"y2":580},{"id":"steplab","kind":"text","color":"#d0402b","width":2,"x":610,"y":420,"size":44,"text":"step opposite the slope"}],"beats":[{"id":"b1","narration":"Gradient descent finds a curve's lowest point.","reveals":["xaxis","yaxis","xlab","flab","curve","mindot","minlab"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b2","narration":"Start at three, height nine.","reveals":["dot","dotlab","tangent"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b3","narration":"Step opposite the slope, downhill, toward zero.","reveals":["step","steplab"],"pauseFrames":15}]},{"schema":"whiteboard-scene/1","sceneId":"s2","primitives":[{"id":"graph","kind":"graph","color":"#1f3a93","width":4,"x":1080,"y":160,"w":760,"h":760,"domain":[-3.5,3.5],"range":[0,12.25],"points":[[-3.5,12.25],[-3,9],[-2.5,6.25],[-2,4],[-1.5,2.25],[-1,1],[-0.5,0.25],[0,0],[0.5,0.25],[1,1],[1.5,2.25],[2,4],[2.5,6.25],[3,9],[3.5,12.25]]},{"id":"rule1","kind":"text","color":"#222222","width":3,"x":80,"y":200,"size":64,"text":"slope = 2x"},{"id":"rule2","kind":"text","color":"#222222","width":3,"x":80,"y":320,"size":56,"text":"new x = x − 0.25 × slope"},{"id":"dot1","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d35400","width":6,"cx":1786,"cy":362,"rx":12,"ry":12},{"id":"lab1","kind":"text","color":"#d35400","width":3,"x":1808,"y":340,"size":40,"text":"9"},{"id":"step1a","kind":"text","color":"#c0392b","width":3,"x":80,"y":480,"size":52,"text":"x = 3, slope 6"},{"id":"step1b","kind":"text","color":"#c0392b","width":3,"x":80,"y":560,"size":52,"text":"new x = 3 − 1.5 = 1.5"},{"id":"arr1","kind":"arrow","color":"#c0392b","width":5,"x1":1776,"y1":378,"x2":1632,"y2":764},{"id":"dot2","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d35400","width":6,"cx":1623,"cy":780,"rx":12,"ry":12},{"id":"lab2","kind":"text","color":"#d35400","width":3,"x":1648,"y":770,"size":40,"text":"2.25"},{"id":"step2a","kind":"text","color":"#27ae60","width":3,"x":80,"y":700,"size":52,"text":"x = 1.5, slope 3"},{"id":"step2b","kind":"text","color":"#27ae60","width":3,"x":80,"y":780,"size":52,"text":"new x = 1.5 − 0.75 = 0.75"},{"id":"arr2","kind":"arrow","color":"#27ae60","width":5,"